-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785931184952754001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"016d44ca-7e60-4157-a6f4-6d144d6b374f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4ca2-97b4-51fb-41c9"}],"description":"Discovered while attesting 4ca2 AC5 (structured-output-baseline run 31003041092). Under the matrix proxy harness (SENTINEL_DIRECTIVE appended to bare production prompts), live marker adoption was 0/20 across anthropic/bedrock/openai: models honored the 'single object, no fence' clause (which improved parse success: anthropic 6->12, bedrock 9->11) but did NOT emit the literal <<<REBAR_OUTPUT>>>/<<<END>>> markers. The E2 compliance fact (16/16 sonnet/haiku on Bedrock) was measured under the REAL schema_directive path (SENTINEL_DIRECTIVE trailing the schema directive), not this bare-prompt append; the proxy under-measures compliance and the 'Then wrap...' lead-in dangles when appended to a bare prompt. The parser's fail-closed NO-DECOY-WIN safety is proven offline and does not depend on live adoption, so this is a reliability improvement, not a defect. Options: strengthen/rephrase SENTINEL_DIRECTIVE for bare-prompt robustness, add a one-shot marker example, or align the matrix 'sentinel' variant with the real schema_directive path. Acceptance: a live measurement shows marker adoption materially >0 on at least anthropic+bedrock without regressing parse-success.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"reconciler","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d85c6d07-8beb-4fd1-a9d8-8cc6bf1e3df7","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],